# no-deferral.waivers — the committed allowlist for scripts/no-deferral-gate.sh.
#
# FORMAT:  <MATCHER><whitespace><reason>
#   MATCHER is either an EXACT `path:line`, or a PATH GLOB (any matcher with no trailing `:<digits>`).
#   A marker (file:line) is WAIVED when an exact row equals it, or a glob row matches its file.
# The allowlist is a FLOOR CHECKED BOTH WAYS: a marker not waived is RED (over-count); a waiver that
# matches no marker is RED (stale — the marker was resolved). See scripts/no-deferral-gate.sh header
# and docs/design/playbook/gate-no-deferral.md.
#
# --strict-done (what scripts/verify-1.6.0-done.sh runs) additionally FAILS if ANY row below is not a
# */hot/* row: the hot/* foundation fixtures are the ONE permanent exemption; the voice skeleton rows
# are TRACKED 1.6.0 debt that MUST be gone before 1.6.0 is done.

# ── PERMANENT: the plane-ABI foundation compile-surface fixtures (out-of-1.6.0-scope) ──────────────
# ~51 unimplemented!() sites in `mod stub` / PlaneHostVtable::STUB / PlaneDecl::STUB, plus the
# PlaneDecl::STUB doc-comment reference. These are ADDITIVE and UNUSED — nothing in the engine calls
# them (hot/mod.rs); a STUB vtable slot panics BY DESIGN. They type-check that every extern "C-unwind"
# ABI fn-pointer slot has a real, well-typed signature. Their real hosts are the protocols-as-plugins
# effort (docs/design/1.6.0-protocols-as-plugins.md), not a voice/1.6.0-GA blocker.
crates/busbar-plugin/src/hot/*   plane-ABI foundation compile-surface fixtures (STUB): additive/unused, never dispatched; out-of-1.6.0-scope (protocols-as-plugins effort)

# ── TRACKED 1.6.0 DEBT: busbar-voice ships today as a declared SKELETON ────────────────────────────
# Plane 4 (voice) is FULL-scope in 1.6.0 but ships today with handler: None / verbs: &[] and its live
# runtime behind #[cfg(feature = "runtime")] (OFF by default), not installed in the binary. These 12
# SKELETON / "dev-only until DoD" marker lines are HARD DEBT: when voice ships they MUST be removed AND
# the state assertion (real handler, real verbs, runtime compiled in, PLANE_DECL installed) must pass.
# --strict-done FAILS while any of these rows remain, so "1.6.0 done" mechanically requires them gone.
